INT. EMERGENCY ROOM - TRAUMA BAY ONE - NIGHT

Harsh light. Beeping monitors. A gurney in the center, a man under a blood-soaked sheet.

DR. AGNES FALK (40s, scrubs, loupes pushed up on her head) cuts away a sleeve. NURSE DESHAWN (30s, gloves to the elbow) hangs a bag of saline. PARAMEDIC LU (30s, vest, radio on shoulder) pumps the chest. RESIDENT OTTO (20s, pale, shaking) fumbles with a central line kit. The patient, MR. BELLWEATHER (70s, gray stubble, oxygen mask), gasps.

FALK
Pressure?

DESHAWN
Seventy over forty.

FALK
Otto, line.

OTTO
Yes, Doctor. Trying.

FALK
Try faster.

LU
Sinus tach. He's crashing.

BELLWEATHER
(muffled)
Don't... let me...

FALK
Stay with us, Mr. Bellweather.

Alarm. The monitor flatlines. Lu's hands lock on the chest. Falk grabs the paddles.

FALK (CONT'D)
Charge to two hundred. Clear.

Everyone steps back. The body jolts. The line wobbles. Wobbles. Steadies.

DESHAWN
We have a rhythm.

OTTO
(exhaling)
Oh, thank God.

LU
Doctor, he's coding again.

FALK
Again.

Another jolt. The curtain parts. DR. ASHFORD (50s, silver hair, a surgeon's cap, calm as ice) steps in, tying a mask behind his head.

ASHFORD
I'll take over, Dr. Falk.

FALK
Dr. Ashford? He's mine.

ASHFORD
Not anymore. Otto, step aside.

Otto drops the line kit and flattens himself against the wall. Ashford takes the paddles from Falk with a gentle but absolute hand.

ASHFORD (CONT'D)
Charge three-sixty.

DESHAWN
Charged.

ASHFORD
Clear.

The body arches. The monitor sings. Falk lets out a breath, and for the first time looks at her own trembling hands.
